    "title": "October 1 recap: Rapid City news you may have missed today",
    "text": "October 1 recap: Rapid City news you may have missed today\nThursday's news: What you missed while you were at work.\n(10) updates to this series since\nThe 2023 robberies were eight days from each other.\nSturgis' Ruben Bokegard posted a 16:29.7 to win the boys' varsity race, while Custer's Mikayla Dennis ran a 20:15.2 to win the girls' varsity race at the Sturgis Invite.\nCounty commissioners makes changes to library funding, Cost-of-Living Adjustment and Capital Projects before approving the 2027 county budget.\nPennington County Auditor Sabrina Green told the Journal she will be stepping away as the auditor on Nov. 6.\n“Meet the missionaries. We want you to have an encouraging, inspiring, uplifting time. (We hope) everyone will … have a greater understanding of what God is doing in the world.”\nRudy Gibney was born and raised in Dublin. Here's why he traded living in the Irish capital for Wall.\nFind something to do in the area.\nFind something to do in the area.\nThe latest boys soccer schedule and scores for Black Hills schools.\nThe latest girls soccer schedule and scores for Black Hills schools.",
